{
  "requirement": "Habeas's bundled agent instructions MUST tell agents that coverage artifacts\nunder {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.storage`, including profiles, reports,\nand captured source snapshots, are disposable build output and MUST NOT be\nstaged or committed to Git.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** `requirements.test-coverage.guidance.artifacts` says the bundled agent instructions MUST tell agents two things. Coverage artifacts under the `storage` location (profiles, reports, captured source snapshots) are disposable build output. Agents MUST NOT stage or commit them to Git. The `storage` requirement is cited as context only.\n\n**Test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_default_to_process_coverage_and_keep_artifacts_disposable]` is the marked test. Its assertions cover the obligation as follows.\n\n- **Skills that carry the guidance.** For `habeas`, `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`, the whitespace-collapsed bundled skill text (`SKILL.md` plus its references, via `bundled_skill`) must contain \"disposable\" and \"Cargo target directory\". Its lowercased form must contain \"never stage or commit\".\n- **Pointer wording in the other two skills.** For `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`, `assert_text` requires the exact pointer sentence \"Follow the habeas skill's \"Testing and coverage artifacts\": default to `habeas coverage` …\". I read the sources. That sentence sits in the same paragraph as \"never stage or commit disposable coverage artifacts in the Cargo target directory\". \"Disposable\" and \"never stage or commit\" appear in those two skills only in that paragraph, so the generic checks do bind to it.\n- **Home skill.** `habeas` must contain \"Profiles, reports, and captured source\" and `target/habeas/coverage/`. These name the artifact kinds and the storage location. In `assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md` they sit in the same paragraph as \"disposable build artifacts. Never stage or commit them to Git\".\n- **SOP.** The `agent-sops/approved-implementation.sop.md` text is asserted in full: \"profiles, reports, and source snapshots under the Cargo target directory are disposable build output: never stage or commit them to Git\".\n\n**Possible concerns, none a gap.**\n- The home-skill assertions are separate substring checks rather than one sentence match. In practice the phrases occur only in the relevant paragraph, so removing or changing the guidance would fail the test. The SOP and pointer checks are tighter.\n- `habeas-requirements` and `habeas-refactor` are not checked, and they have no coverage-artifact guidance. The text requires the bundled instructions to tell agents, not every skill to repeat it. The home skill, the two pointing skills and the SOP deliver it, and the test checks all of them.\n\n**Result.** I found no obligation that is untested and no assertion that contradicts the requirement. There are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments to account for.",
  "references": "0fe66373f599880ea97b9de591948b4d4a6a583dd2b16af10dccdfce984d9839",
